+- **Yawning per-turn function (closed, #359 P2, static).** `0213F6B0` is a one-line trampoline through the pool pointer `DAT_0213F6C0`, called as `(entity, 0x19, 1)`; it is an effect or display call and changes no status. The yawn-to-sleep conversion is `0218FE64` case 4. [blue-verified, static]
+- **Wake on hit (static reading, #359 P2).** `0217D5FC` calls `0218F21C` (at `0217D648`) and `0218F1EC` (at `0217D790`). `0218F21C` runs the frozen-class end `0218FC18` when `+0xA0` is 6, and `0218FE64(…,0,1)` when `+0x99` is 1 and `+0x9A` is `0x7F`. `0218F1EC` is used for `+0x99` of 1, 3 or 5 with `+0x9A` = `0x7F`; it clears `+0x99` and `+0x9A`. So both act only on the permanent value `0x7F`, and a timed sleep is not woken by damage. [blue-verified, static; the runtime check (hit a slept target, read `+0x99` and `+0x9A`) is still open]
+- **Countdown gate (#359 P2, static; runtime open).** `TickStatusAndHealthRegen` (`02185C70`) has no gate on the call site. Its gates are: entity valid (`02142AE4`), floor not over (`0214067C` is 0), and per class `status != 0` and `0219BF1C` reaching 0. `0219BF1C` leaves `0x7F` alone. [blue-verified, static] **Lead:** the #191 observation likely means each call ticks a different entity and only the `02140BA4` call had the status bearer. Check by logging r0 at each call site.
